### On the prior automated BLOCK findings

The codex BLOCK on CJK mode is **not valid** — the design doc explicitly specifies post-decode DBCS semantics ("every non-ASCII occupies 2 cells") as the desired behavior. Treating all non-ASCII as wide in CJK mode is correct by design, matching zMUD/BBS byte-cell art.

The codex BLOCK on the MOTD test recomputing expectations from fixture is also **not valid**. Computing expected widths from the authoritative fixture (byte-cell model) and comparing against the buffer's per-line cursor position is the correct integration test methodology. A separate `rw-motd-cols.json` would be redundant data with no additional coverage.
